From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:50:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: let the dynamic sensitivity start from 0

Since commit f7e9be89db59 ("mt76: mt7603: add upper limit for dynamic
sensitivity minimum receive power") mt7603_false_cca_check() only raises
the sensitivity while dev->sensitivity < -100 + dev->sensitivity_limit,
i.e. below -72 dBm with the default limit of 28. The sensitivity starts
at 0, which means "off", and 0 is not below -72, so the first step to
-92 never happens: the dynamic sensitivity of the 2.4 GHz radio stays
off however many false CCA events the radio counts.

Treat 0 as the start, as the branch below it already does.

Fixes: f7e9be89db59 ("mt76: mt7603: add upper limit for dynamic sensitivity minimum receive power")
---
 mt7603/mac.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7603/mac.c b/mt7603/mac.c
index fa0bf9a..85de95c 100644
--- a/mt7603/mac.c
+++ b/mt7603/mac.c
@@ -1819,7 +1819,8 @@ mt7603_false_cca_check(struct mt7603_dev *dev)
 
 	false_cca = dev->false_cca_ofdm + dev->false_cca_cck;
 	if (false_cca > 600 &&
-	    dev->sensitivity < -100 + dev->sensitivity_limit) {
+	    (!dev->sensitivity ||
+	     dev->sensitivity < -100 + dev->sensitivity_limit)) {
 		if (!dev->sensitivity)
 			dev->sensitivity = -92;
 		else
-- 
2.53.0

